00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:01.640
So let's start by like
a question that I had

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:02.870
when I was planning this thing.

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:05.135
It was like the only thing
I've never worked in a startup.

00:08:05.135 --> 00:08:06.270
And the only thing I have in mind

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:09.970
is the very Californian vibe of like,

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:11.520
ooh, everybody's working on a scooter,

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:12.660
they have free cafeteria.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:13.870
That's my vision of startups,

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:16.010
which I know it's, that's entirely true.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:19.710
Can you take a crack at what
it's like to work at a startup

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:24.710
and what differentiate a startup
look a more formal company

00:08:24.904 --> 00:08:29.143
and what's your day-to-day
like, who wants to start?

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:32.690
You can just unmute and go.

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:33.540
- I can go first.

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:37.490
Yeah so yeah, there are
plenty of the startups,

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.270
like the Silicon Valley of Styles.

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:42.300
We are a little bit different, more lanes,

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:44.370
no noise scooters for us.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.470
But I think the biggest
things that differentiates

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:50.160
between the startups and
industry jobs, that I'm sure

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.380
you guys will cover in a month or so

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:56.130
is the combination of the
flexibilities you get.

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:59.230
Like, we don't have any time
who comes in, what time,

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:00.130
who lives in time?

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:01.330
No one cares about these things.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.410
No one cares about how
many days you take off

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:04.810
or like what you do.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:08.420
All we care about are the
general milestones that we have

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:10.380
and the things you want to achieve.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:14.687
And the startup is usually a
much more collaborative space.

00:09:14.687 --> 00:09:17.970
It's not like an industry that
the mission is already built,

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:20.220
defined, and usually
everything is designed

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:21.910
to optimize the revenue.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:24.220
For example, whatever the businesses.

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:29.220
In our case and in most startups,
you're still figuring out

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:30.670
what the mission is even gonna be.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:34.170
So every player, everyone
who joins the company

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:37.570
is less of an employee
more often by all means

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:38.860
and purposes of teammate,

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:41.130
because everyone needs to work together

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:45.480
and everyone needs to have
several hats to the final goal.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:46.860
So it's a little bit less boring

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:49.270
when it gets to the job
roles that you have.

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:52.090
You get to pick, you can
switch for a lot of projects.

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:55.090
Anytime you start a new, or
if you have a better idea

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:56.260
for how to do the projects,

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:59.490
any case like developing
the Quantum stuff,

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:02.100
if you have a better idea of
people are there to listen.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:05.960
Things are not set in stone,
but of course it always comes

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:09.160
with this bigger risk
that it is a startup.

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:11.430
You always wondering, like
what happens in a year,

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:13.580
in two years when he
gets to like the fundings

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:14.510
and everything like that.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:17.643
So it has its own plus and minuses.

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:23.913
- Sure, I guess I'm next.

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:27.570
So I think a lot of it was covered already

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:31.810
to add to that a startup
coming from industry

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:35.403
or big corporations,
there is more structure.

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:39.860
So for example, what this
means is in a big corporation,

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:42.660
when there's a feature we often go through

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:46.000
and have a whole like session
where you discussed this

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.450
with like the managers, the business side,

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:50.170
they will approve this feature.

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:51.530
And then finally, when it gets to you,

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:54.400
it's definitely gonna
be that it won't change.

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:55.260
There's no, like...

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:59.120
There's always a very clear
like map of everything

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:00.960
that you need on by the end of this week

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:03.360
or this iteration or the sprint.

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:05.680
Start-ups is a little bit more free

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:09.300
in the sense that we try to keep up...

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:11.550
We try to keep like a structure as well

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:13.150
for iterations, for example.

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:16.040
But due to the fact that we work closely

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:19.320
with like the hardware
engineers who use our software,

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:22.770
we at the same time are also
production support for them.

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:25.130
'Cause it's not like we
have a separate team for it.

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:26.610
And when features come in,

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:29.810
they sometimes get prioritize in one way.

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:32.580
But as we're going
through this might change

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.930
due to various reasons.

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:37.530
Could be because people
want one thing sooner,

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:40.480
it could be because we just
like wanted to switch it

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:42.560
'cause it wasn't as because some feature,

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:44.610
wasn't as important as this other one.

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:49.270
So the structure behind a
startup, it's a little more free.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:51.330
This is good or bad, it depends.

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:53.400
You get used to the flow over time,

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.500
but coming in, you might
be a little overwhelmed,

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:57.850
like, wait, we were supposed to deliver

00:11:57.850 --> 00:11:59.580
this for this upcoming iteration,

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:01.640
but now it's like taken out entirely.

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:03.623
Don't think about it until next iteration.

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:07.940
- Yes Victor.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:10.810
- Yeah, can I have just a warning.

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:11.643
- Yeah.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:17.170
- I do agree, with our colleagues here,

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:20.320
when will you compare
the work of a startup

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:23.740
to the work inside a corporation?

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:26.963
The work in a corporation
seems kind of mundane.

00:12:27.858 --> 00:12:32.858
It can be boring even it's
exciting to work with startups.

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:38.390
And as as they were saying,

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:41.970
different hats, adapting to change.

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:45.063
My only warning is that oftentimes,

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:49.823
all these, innovation and exciting,

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:54.700
I would say behavior within startups

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:58.970
can be easily just be innovation theater.

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:03.144
And you gave the appearance
that everything is,

00:13:03.144 --> 00:13:05.770
working towards the goal, et cetera,

00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:08.660
but you're just, not
necessarily progressing

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:10.380
towards actual change.

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:12.380
And so that's my only warning,

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:14.860
sometimes founders will come your way

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:17.670
and they will promise heaven to you,

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:21.860
and you can actually decide
to follow their footsteps,

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:24.570
but you will go down instead of up.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:29.210
So be careful I'm not buying
just innovation theater

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:32.140
and make sure that you're
really buying into a vision

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:35.380
that has a lot of execution involved.

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:38.820
It's my only warning, I
think innovation can be found

00:13:38.820 --> 00:13:40.930
in multiple spaces within corporations

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:44.800
as well with startups.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:48.037
- So to jump on that,
what are the key signs

00:13:48.037 --> 00:13:50.680
